  "worked_solution": "A function $g(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}g(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty,tz) & =2(tx)^{2}+(tx)(ty)^{2}+5(tz)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{3}x{y}^{2}+5{t}^{2}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}g(x,y,z)={t}^{n}(2{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+5{z}^{2})\n$$\n\nand so $g(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
